      source: "Photograph of Marianne North standing on the doorstep of her house at Alderley, Gloucestershire, by her neighbour Mrs. Bryan Hodgson, taken soon after North arrived there in 1886 and printed as the frontispiece to volume 2 of Recollections of a Happy Life (London and New York: Macmillan; Internet Archive scan recollectionsofh02nortuoft, University of Toronto copy, Macmillan 1894 printing, whose first edition appeared in 1892). The plate carries North's own handwritten caption 'Marianne North at home, Mount House, Alderley, May to November as long as life lasts'. Her sister's preface states that the frontispiece shows her on the doorstep of her house at Alderley, was done by a neighbour, Mrs. Bryan Hodgson, on her first arrival there, and bears her signature. The file is the Wikimedia Commons extract of the page (1688 x 2904 pixels), cropped to the photograph (caption and margins removed) and downscaled to 696 x 1000, with no upscaling.",
